% CODA, bars 333-384.
% 333-348 Più mosso: motive x as a stretto ostinato entering from the bottom (Vc 333, Vla 334, Vln II 335, Vln I 336), pp crescendo; the bass falls
%   E-D-C sharp-B (337-340); theme A's head ff (341); Vln I peaks on B6 at 344 (the scherzo's highest note, a semitone under the finale's C7);
%   hemiola cadence 345-346, E minor chord ff (347), general pause (348).
% 349-384 Meno mosso (tempo del Trio), T returns p in Hn 1 (349), Cl 1 (353), Vln I and Fl 1 (357), cadence 363.
%   c013: T's first half (349-356) is in A major, the tonicized IV that a late coda can carry (Aldwell-Schachter Unit 26 sec. 11, PDF 451-452);
%   its half cadence on E (356, V of A) is the pivot back to E (I), and T's second half (357-364) confirms E with ii-ii6-6/4-V-I.
% 365-368: Hn 1 sings the motto's chromatic tail on the fifth degree, B-A sharp-A-G sharp (E flat-D-D flat-C transposed),
%   over E - A sharp dim7 - A minor (iv, mixture) - E: a plagal close that ends on G sharp.
% 369-384: E major held pp, then only Hn 1 and Vln I on G sharp (the pitch that opened the scherzo, movement II's A flat) over a timpani roll
%   and a last pizzicato E; the finale can take that G sharp as A flat.

